\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces KaryoFlow overview. (a) RF replaces the curved DDPM trajectory with a straight-line ODE path from noise $x_1$ to GT box $x_0$; nodes = $4$ solver steps. (b) Time conditioning via AdaLN-Zero zero-initialized modulation (identity at $t{=}0$). (c) Coupling: Random pairing (orange) keeps full diversity $H(V \mid X_t){=}\log K$; Sinkhorn-based Stochastic OT (pink) interpolates between hard OT and Random ($0 < H < \log K$).}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
