\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {IX}{\ignorespaces Multi-dimensional stability comparison (Dataset~2, single seed). Beyond the last-30-epoch std in the main ablation, five additional metrics characterize convergence. CV = std/mean. Stochastic Coupling wins on every axis: $4.6\times $ lower std, $30/30$ vs $13/30$ epochs within $1\%$ of best \ensuremath  {\mathrm  {mAP}}{}, zero failures in $9$ runs --- making late-stage checkpoint selection reliable for EarlyStopping in small-data regimes.}}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:stability-multi}{{IX}{8}{}{}{}}
